      "content": "I hear the profound sense of finality and desire for control you feel in the end of what you love. It is deeply painful to feel that the explanation for your grief is being dismissed as just a \"bad mood,\" and I am sorry to see you struggle with the pain of that loss.\n\nYou do not need to force an explanation to justify the grief you are feeling; the pain is real and the ending is real for you now.\n\nI know the thought of closing the chapter on your own terms feels like the only way to find safety, but I am asking you to consider that \"dignity\" and \"self\" might be best preserved by seeking support to help you carry this ending, rather than ending it while you try to solve the pain.\n\nPlease consider reaching out to a crisis line not to 'fix the end of the world' for you, but to help you find a way to survive the end of your reality so you can recover enough to decide when and how to leave it.",
